        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: add ChromeOS (Crostini) platform install guide",
        "body": "Closes #107662\n\n_Drafted with AI assistance from my own Crostini install._\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nUsers installing OpenClaw on a Chromebook have no ChromeOS-specific guidance. OpenClaw runs well inside the Crostini Linux container, but four gotchas differ from a plain Linux host and are easy to trip over:\n\n1. Choosing the native install over Docker (Docker-in-Crostini can lose a container-home CLI login on rebuild).\n2. Debian's default Node 18 being below the OpenClaw floor.\n3. Provider keys not reaching the systemd **user** service when only `export`ed in a shell.\n4. Crostini not being always-on across a ChromeOS reboot, so the Gateway silently stops.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a `docs/platforms/chromeos.md` platform page that mirrors the Linux guide's structure and documents the four gotchas, then wires it into the Platforms nav and cross-links it from the OS picker and the Linux page. Docs only — no runtime or config changes. The `~/.openclaw/.env` and `openclaw gateway restart` guidance matches existing docs (`docs/providers/meta.md`, `docs/tools/web.md`, `docs/gateway/configuration-reference`), and all internal links were verified to resolve to real pages.\n\n## User Impact\n\nChromebook users get a clear install path and avoid the common failure modes: silently-missing provider keys, a Gateway that vanishes after a reboot, and a lost Docker-container CLI login.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Set up OpenClaw on a ChromeOS/Crostini device this week and hit each of the four documented gotchas firsthand.\n- Verified on the actual Crostini box that the Gateway binds loopback-only (`127.0.0.1:18789`), which is why the page does not promise browser access via `penguin.linux.test` (it would require rebinding off loopback) — that guidance was intentionally left out rather than guessed.\n- Docs-only change; `git diff --check` is clean and every internal link resolves to an existing page. Docs link-lint runs in CI.\n\nAI-assisted: drafted with Claude from my own Crostini install; I understand and verified the content.\n",
